  Quote of the Week:

  German philosopher George Hegel, 1821:
  "In England even the poorest of people believe they have Rights; this is 
very different from what satisfies the poor in other lands."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:

  In spring, Hokuto cast a Flood spell and Balmwood was magically flooded.
  In early summer, Hokuto attempted an illegal move.  He tried to move from 
Balmwood to Silvermist, but provincial flooding and insufficient transport 
thwarted the move.  Instead, Hokuto invented nothing worthy of note in his 
sagely researches.
  Midsummer's night came and went and a hot late summer arrived.  Hokuto 
tried to move from Balmwood to Cretacia, a non-adjacent province.  This is 
illegal!  Instead, Hokuto practiced his Psychic Magic well, and even 
consulted an astrologer, but could not improve his skill in Psychic Magic.
  With the advent of the fall season, Hokuto cast a Bless spell.  Cretacia 
was magically blessed and prospered.  The Bless affected no armies in 
Cretacia.
  During early winter, Hokuto failed in his attempt to cast a Bless spell.

  Thus endeth the adventures of Hokuto for this year.


  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  Kokocala (#10) has arrived in Kilkenny from Ravenwood.
  Inanna (#85) heard that an old buddy was trapping furs in Dirkwood and 
left Kilkenny to see her old friend.
  The 212th Camel Corps helped a local count of Starhaven to subdue a 
rebellious baron and rose to Crack quality.


  Here is the financial report for Hokuto's kingdom: this turn, the Kingdom 
collected 46 gold in revenue.  3 gold was expended to finance our leaders.  
The 10th Light Cavalry, the 112th Bowmen, the 113th Light Cavalry, the 154th 
Legion and the 278th Axemen trained well and improved in quality.  44 gold 
was expended to maintain our armies.  Hokuto was left with 6 gold in the 
treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Ningarl
To: Hokuto

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Stormy winter melted into sweet spring, and I prepared to carry out my 
urgent assignments.  I recruited enough men in Cretacia to form the 278th 
Axemen and the 10th Light Cavalry for the army of Ningarl.
  With the coming of the early summer season I boldly marched my command 
into Cherrywood (#501).
  In late summer, I levied the 112th Bowmen and the 113th Light Cavalry from 
among the people of Cherrywood, to serve under me.
  The hot days of summer mellowed into a colorful fall.  I attempted a Bless 
spell, but bungled it.
  With the advent of the early winter season I moved into St Helens (#402) 
with my redoubtable army.

  Thy humble servant,   Ningarl


From: Lexington
To: Hokuto

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I cast a Bless spell.  Amberleaf was magically blessed and 
prospered.  The skeletal remains of the 39th Axemen and the 40th Axemen were 
Blessed and permanently destroyed.
  In early summer, I marched on Cretacia (#601) with my forces.
  Midsummer's day passed and a pleasant late summer arrived.  I boldly 
marched my forces into Starhaven (#701).
  With the advent of the fall season, I recruited the 172nd Legion, the 
191st Legion and the 192nd Chariots from among the population of Starhaven, 
to serve under me.
  In early winter, I worked on my Element Magic but was thwarted in my 
efforts.

  Thy humble servant,   Lexington


